<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en-US"><head><meta charSet="utf-8" data-next-head=""/><style data-fullcalendar="true" data-next-head=""></style><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" data-next-head=""/><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8" data-next-head=""/><meta name="service" content="web-next" data-next-head=""/><meta name="X-Location" content="east" data-next-head=""/><meta name="X-Build-Version" content="ccd1aebcde5d2dfdbf081f86deedb26c82a71fdb" data-next-head=""/><link rel="icon" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/favicon.ico" type="image/x-icon" sizes="any" data-next-head=""/><link rel="shortcut icon" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/favicon.ico" data-next-head=""/><link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="120x120" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/general/m_redesign_120x120.png" data-next-head=""/><link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="152x152" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/general/m_redesign_152x152.png" data-next-head=""/><link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="167x167" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/general/m_redesign_167x167.png" data-next-head=""/><link rel="shortcut icon" sizes="128x128" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/general/m_redesign_128x128.png" data-next-head=""/><link rel="shortcut icon" sizes="196x196" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/general/m_redesign_196x196.png" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="/_next/static/media/NeuSans-Regular.1ca3b39b.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin="anonymous" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="/_next/static/media/NeuSans-Medium.7b11edcf.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin="anonymous" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="/_next/static/media/NeuSans-Bold.5c45f750.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin="anonymous" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="/_next/static/media/NeuSans-Book.27256a60.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin="anonymous" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="/_next/static/media/Boyrun-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin="anonymous" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://www.facebook.com/tr?id=792405807634160&amp;ev=PageView&amp;noscript=1" as="image" data-next-head=""/><script type="application/ld+json" data-next-head="">{"@type":"Organization","@context":"https://schema.org","url":"https://www.meetup.com/find/","name":"Meetup","logo":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/general/m_redesign_630x630.png","sameAs":["https://www.facebook.com/meetup/","https://twitter.com/Meetup/","https://www.youtube.com/meetup","https://www.instagram.com/meetup/"]}</script><title data-next-head="">Find Events &amp; Groups | Meetup</title><meta name="description" content="Find Meetup events and groups so you can do more of what matters to you and meet people near you who share your interests." data-next-head=""/><meta property="fb:app_id" content="2403839689" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:site_name" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:type" content="article" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:title" content="Find Events &amp; Groups | Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:description" content="Find Meetup events and groups so you can do more of what matters to you and meet people near you who share your interests." data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:url" content="https://www.meetup.com/find/" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:image" content="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/shared/meetup-flyer.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:android:app_name" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:android:package" content="com.meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:ios:app_store_id" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:ios:app_name" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:web:should_fallback" content="true" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:android:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:ios:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:web:url" content="https://www.meetup.com/" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:site" content="@meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:image" content="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/shared/meetup-flyer.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:description" content="Find Meetup events and groups so you can do more of what matters to you and meet people near you who share your interests." data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:iphone" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:iphone" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:ipad" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:ipad" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:googleplay" content="com.meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:googleplay" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" data-next-head=""/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.meetup.com/find/" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><script type="application/ld+json" data-next-head="">[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"UXNight: How Teams Design AI Tools","url":"https://www.meetup.com/cascadesf/events/316875083/","description":"\\*\\*\\*\\*Please note: A ticket must be purchased through Luma to attend this event. An RSVP without a ticket does not guarantee admission.\\*\\*\n**Get tickets at [luma.com/designaitools](luma.com/designaitools)**\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\n# UXNight is back. And UX is entering a whole new era.\n\n**AI is changing how we design, what we design, and what it means to create great user experiences.**\n\nAs intelligent products and AI agents reshape the digital landscape, UXNight returns to bring designers, researchers, and product leaders together to explore what's next.\n\nFor our return, **Cascade SF is teaming up with Superhuman** for an evening exploring how teams across the company design AI-powered products, collaborate across disciplines, and create agentic experiences for everyday users.\n\n**Come for the insights, stay for the connections!** Enjoy food and refreshments sponsored by Superhuman, connect with fellow designers and product leaders, and stop by our special **Aura Photography Booth** for a unique, colorful portrait to capture the evening.\n\n## How Teams Design AI Tools\n\nWhat does it take to design AI products when the technology, user expectations, and design practices are all evolving at once?\nHear directly from Superhuman's design and research leaders as they share the challenges they're tackling, the workflows they're developing, and what they're learning along the way.\nFrom designing intuitive AI agents to scaling research and building user trust, we'll explore how different disciplines contribute to creating AI experiences that are useful, approachable, and grounded in real human needs.\n**Explore the ideas, challenges, and emerging practices shaping the next era of AI product design.**\n\n## Featured Talks\n\n**\"Designing Agents for the Everyday User\"**\nPhil Vander Broek · Head of Design, Superhuman Go\n**\"Researchers, Build Your Own Table: Scaling Influence in the Age of AI\"**\nJosh Williams · Director of Product Research, Superhuman\n**\"Designing for Trust with AI\"**\nApril Littrell · Senior Content Designer, Growth Design, Superhuman\n\n## What We'll Explore\n\n* Designing intuitive, useful AI agents for everyday users\n* How AI is transforming design and research workflows\n* Scaling research to keep pace with faster product development\n* Collaboration across design, research, product, and leadership\n* Building trust through transparency, voice, and content design\n\n**For product designers, UX researchers, content designers, design leaders, and anyone building AI products.**\n\n***\n\n# Announced Sessions\n\n## \"Designing Agents for the Everyday User\"\n\n**Phil Vander Broek, Head of Design at Superhuman Go**\n\nAI agents are going mainstream, but many of today's interaction patterns were developed for technical users. How do we make agents intuitive and useful for everyone, from marketers and sales teams to students?\nSuperhuman Go is an AI coworker designed to understand your work and help you get things done wherever you work. Phil Vander Broek will share what his team is learning as they bring agentic experiences to everyday users.\n**What you'll learn:**\n\n* **Introducing the agent mental model:** How onboarding helps users understand an AI coworker and gradually discover its capabilities.\n* **Designing for control:** How users delegate work to agents while staying informed and in charge.\n* **Making agents accessible:** Approaches to discovering, creating, and using agents without technical expertise.\n* **Balancing proactivity and autonomy:** How to design agents that know when to help and when to stay out of the way.\n\nYou'll leave with emerging design patterns, practical lessons, and a clearer understanding of the challenges shaping the next generation of agentic experiences.\n\n***\n\n## \"Researchers, Build Your Own Table: Scaling Influence in the Age of AI\"\n\n**Josh Williams, Director of Product Research at Superhuman**\n\nAI is accelerating product development. But as teams move faster, how can researchers ensure that meaningful insights continue to influence what gets built?\nJosh Williams will share how Superhuman's research team is rethinking its tools, systems, and workflows to increase research's impact across the organization.\nDrawing from real examples, he'll explore how the team is using AI to analyze findings, connect evidence, and make research more accessible and actionable.\n**What you'll learn:**\n\n* **Building shared research systems:** Create infrastructure that makes findings easier to organize, discover, and reuse.\n* **Accelerating analysis with AI:** Use emerging tools to synthesize findings and uncover connections across research.\n* **Making insights actionable:** Help product teams access evidence and apply it to decisions.\n* **Expanding research's influence:** Develop workflows that give researchers more capacity to connect insights, guide strategy, and support faster-moving teams.\n\nDiscover how AI can help researchers move beyond delivering findings to building systems that amplify their influence across product development.\n\n***\n\n## \"Designing for Trust with AI\"\n\n**April Littrell, Senior Content Designer, Growth Design, Superhuman**\n\nAI's most powerful tools are becoming friendlier and more approachable. Playful interfaces, warm language, and familiar interactions make sharing our emails, documents, and personal information feel increasingly ordinary.\nBut are we earning people's trust, or simply making it easier to overlook their concerns?\n**How do we make AI approachable without making its consequences easier to overlook?**\n\nApril Littrell explores how content design shapes trust across the user journey, from a brand's first impression to onboarding and everyday product interactions.\nUsing familiar industry examples and the public Superhuman website, she'll examine how voice, product framing, and information architecture influence what people understand, expect, and ultimately trust.\n\n**What you'll learn:**\n\n* **Design for transparency:** Communicate what AI can and can't do, including limitations, uncertainty, and how personal data is used.\n* **Build trust through content:** Use voice, tone, and messaging to make AI approachable without overstating its capabilities.\n* **Align promises with experiences:** Identify gaps between what your product promises, what people understand, and what it actually delivers.\n* **Look beyond conversion:** Understand why signups and activation don't necessarily indicate lasting trust.\n\nConversion rates tell us people signed up or started using our product. They don't tell us whether we've built lasting trust, or a house of cards.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Get tickets while you can at [luma.com/designaitools](luma.com/designaitools)\\*\\*\\***\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\nWant to give a talk? Email \\[andi@cascadesf\\.com\\]\\(mailto: andi@cascadesf\\.com\\)\\.","startDate":"2026-12-03T01:15:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Superhuman","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"San Francisco","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"us","streetAddress":"475 Sansome St, San Francisco, CA 94111, USA, San Francisco, CA"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Cascade SF, Experience Designers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/cascadesf/"},"performer":"Cascade SF, Experience Designers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Hedge West SF December 2026 Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/hedge-west-sf-quant-data-and-ai/events/316558391/","description":"**The next quarterly HedgeWestSF meetup in San Francisco is on December 8, 2026 from 6pm to 9pm. Join us at The House of AI at 40 Boardman Place in San Francisco's West SOMA Neighborhood** **near 7th and Bryant Streets. Parking available at 71 Boardman Place.**\n\nPresentations:\n\n**Vladimir Ofitserov** (REVO Capital - revocm.com) - *Scaling Quant Research with AI*\n\n**Vinesh Jha** (ExtractAlpha - ExtractAlpha.com) - *Advances in Alternate Data Alpha. New research, emerging signals, and what systematic investors should be watching next* (Rescheduled from the last meetup)\n\n**Greg Kapoustin** (validityBase - [vbase.com](https://vbase.com/?utm_source=luma)) - *Why Backtests Aren’t Trusted: Common Mistakes and Their Solutions*\n\nCALL FOR SPONSORS - Help keep HedgeWestSF going by becoming a sponsor - https://hedgewestsf.org/sponsorship\nCALL FOR PRESENTATIONS - Want to present at a future HedgeWestSF? Email hedgewestsf@novumcove.com\n\n**HedgeWestSF is sponsored by Novum Cove Capital Management and ExtractAlpha.**\n\nFood and refreshments will be served. As always, professionals, students, and anyone with an interest in trading, quant, data, and AI in finance are welcome! Looking forward to seeing you there!","startDate":"2026-12-09T02:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"House of AI","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"San Francisco","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"us","streetAddress":"40 Boardman Pl, San Francisco, CA"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Hedge West SF - Quant, Data, and AI","url":"https://www.meetup.com/hedge-west-sf-quant-data-and-ai/"},"performer":"Hedge West SF - Quant, Data, and AI"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Agentics Foundation Meetup - San Francisco","url":"https://www.meetup.com/san-francisco-agentics-foundation-meetups/events/317300969/","description":"🔥 **110 Million Downloads. 200,000 GitHub Stars. One Night in San Francisco.**\n\n​Join the **Agentics Foundation** on **Tuesday, December 1st at 6:30 PM** for an evening of agentic AI, open source, and connections with the people building what comes next.\n\n​Hosted by **Reuven “Ruv” Cohen**, whose open-source projects have collectively reached **110 million downloads and 200,000 GitHub stars**, this gathering brings together developers, founders, researchers, and AI enthusiasts to connect, exchange ideas, and explore what’s possible with AI agents.\n\n​Bring your questions, share what you’re working on, and meet potential collaborators. From your first experiments with vibe coding to building systems for production, there’s a place for you in the conversation.\n\n​🚀 Explore the possibilities of agentic AI\n​🤝 Connect with fellow builders and founders\n​💡 Exchange ideas, challenges, and lessons from real projects\n​🌉 Meet the San Francisco Agentics community\n​\n​**Come curious. Leave connected and ready to build.**\n​\n​📍 **San Francisco**\n​📅 **Tuesday, December 1st, 2026**\n​🕕 **5:30 PM Pacific**","startDate":"2026-12-02T01:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"199 Museum Way","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"San Francisco","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"us","streetAddress":"199 Museum Way, San Francisco, CA 94114, USA, San Francisco, CA"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"San Francisco Agentics Foundation Meetups","url":"https://www.meetup.com/san-francisco-agentics-foundation-meetups/"},"performer":"San Francisco Agentics Foundation Meetups"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"10 Everyday Business Tasks You Can Hand to Claude Today [ONLINE]","url":"https://www.meetup.com/palo-alto-ai-business-vibes/events/317273671/","description":"Most owners use Claude for one or two things and miss the rest. Aida walks Palo Alto owners through everyday tasks Claude handles well, from writing and summarising to planning, using Projects, file uploads and saved instructions.\n\n**What we'll cover:**\n• The five Claude features owners use every day\n• Projects, file uploads and saved instructions explained simply\n• Writing, summarising and planning faster\n• Building your own everyday Claude routine\n\n**Format:** Live on Google Meet with business owners from Palo Alto and the Bridges Network. We work through it together on screen, and questions are answered as we go.\n\n**Who it's for:** owners and managers who have tried Claude but don't use it daily yet.\n\n**Bring:** a laptop and a free Claude account.\n\n**Hosted by:** Aida from the Bridges Network.\n\n**When you RSVP:** two optional questions: whether you would like a free AI consultation, and your phone number if you want an SMS reminder before we start. Both are optional, so skip them if you like.\n\n**Fair to mention:** we end with a brief word about our done-for-you help. Everything above is taught in full beforehand.\n\n**Where:** Google Meet. The link appears here once you RSVP \"Going.\" 45 minutes, no cost.","startDate":"2026-11-30T20:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OnlineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"VirtualLocation","url":"https://www.meetup.com/palo-alto-ai-business-vibes/events/317273671/"},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Palo Alto AI Business Vibes","url":"https://www.meetup.com/palo-alto-ai-business-vibes/"},"performer":"Palo Alto AI Business Vibes"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"San Francisco AI & ML Professionals, Investors and Start-Ups Networking","url":"https://www.meetup.com/sanfrancisco-startup-pitch-and-networking/events/317300525/","description":"🔔 **Please Note:** RSVP on Meetup **does not guarantee entry**.\nTo attend, you **must register through the official ticket link** here: [https://www.eventbrite.com/e/sf-ai-tech-startups-investors-innovators-networking-mixer-tickets-2004164381616](https://www.eventbrite.com/e/sf-ai-tech-startups-investors-innovators-networking-mixer-tickets-2004164381616)\n\nStep into the vibrant world of artificial intelligence and machine learning at our exclusive San Francisco AI & Machine Learnig Network Mixer. This event caters to innovators, thinkers, and investors in the AI and ML spheres, providing a unique opportunity to connect with industry leaders, discover cutting-edge projects, and explore potential collaborations.\n\n**Event Highlights:**\n**One-Minute Presentations:** A rapid-fire session where AI and ML startups can pitch their innovations and business ideas directly to a curated audience of peers and potential investors. Each presentation is limited to one minute, emphasizing clarity and impact.\n**Structured Networking Opportunities:** Engage in meaningful discussions with fellow innovators and industry leaders. This event is designed to foster connections that lead to collaboration, investment, and growth.\n**Investment & Business Growth Opportunities** – Discover potential deals, secure funding, and connect with professionals offering valuable expertise.\n\n**Who Should Attend:**\n\n* **Emerging AI and ML Startups:** Showcase your innovations and seek partnerships or funding in a focused setting.\n* **Investors:** Find pioneering startups within the AI and ML domains that align with your investment criteria.\n* **AI and ML Professionals:** Network with peers, discuss advancements and industry challenges, and potentially find your next career move.\n* **Students and Academics:** Immerse yourself in the industry environment, gain insights, and connect with potential mentors and collaborators.\n\n**Why This Event is a Must:**\n\n* **Effective Networking:** Tailored specifically for the AI and ML communities, this mixer facilitates targeted networking, helping you build meaningful connections that can lead to collaborative projects or ventures.\n* **Opportunity for Exposure:** Startups can gain visibility by presenting their projects during one-minute pitches, directly communicating their value to an audience that includes potential investors and collaborators.\n* **Insight into Industry Trends:** Keep up-to-date with the latest research and commercial opportunities in AI and ML through conversations with industry insiders and thought leaders.\n* **Career Opportunities:** Professionals looking to advance in the AI and ML fields can discover new opportunities and expand their networks in a dynamic, supportive environment.\n\nDon’t miss this opportunity to engage with the forefront of AI and ML innovation. Whether you’re looking to invest, collaborate, or just learn about the next big thing in tech, our San Francisco AI & ML Network Mixer is the place to be. Secure your spot today and be part of shaping the future of technology!\n\n**Why attend:**\n**1-Minute Elevator Pitches:** Every attendee will have the chance to do a **short, 1-minute pitch** to the room — introduce yourself, share what you’re building or working on, and let others know what kind of co-founder, partner, or expertise you’re looking for.\n**Networking**: Experience an evening of dynamic networking in a relaxed and welcoming atmosphere. Meet IT professionals from diverse backgrounds, including software development, cybersecurity, data science, cloud computing, artificial intelligence, and more.\n**Career Advancement Opportunities**: Explore potential career opportunities by interacting with representatives from leading tech companies and startups. Discover the latest job openings and internships in the IT and Technology sectors.\n\nThe event will be held in a sophisticated and vibrant venue, adorned with modern decor and equipped with state-of-the-art facilities to ensure your comfort and convenience throughout the day.\n\n**Register now - space is limited to 50 attendees only!**\n**P.S. Click Follow for future event alerts!**","startDate":"2026-12-09T03:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Hawthorn SF Nightclub and Lounge","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"San Francisco","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"us","streetAddress":"46 Geary St, San Francisco, CA 94108, USA, San Francisco, CA"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"San Francisco Startup Pitch and Networking","url":"https://www.meetup.com/sanfrancisco-startup-pitch-and-networking/"},"performer":"San Francisco Startup Pitch and Networking"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Bay Area AI War Room - Berkeley Edition - Saturday, 10:00 AM","url":"https://www.meetup.com/bay-area-artificial-war-room/events/313150527/","description":"Models, agent, systems, ethics, the law, business, art and impact we discuss it all. With the DeepSeek hoopla fading, what of Reasoning models?\n\nInspired by the Berkeley AI War Room, we invite you to join us at the same venue, same time, and with the same dynamic community.\n\nCome share your interests, showcase your projects, and discuss the latest trends and news that's shaping the AI landscape at a rapid pace.","startDate":"2026-12-05T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Victory Point Cafe","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Berkeley","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"us","streetAddress":"1797 Shattuck Ave. Ste A, Berkeley, CA"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Bay Area AI War Room","url":"https://www.meetup.com/bay-area-artificial-war-room/"},"performer":"Bay Area AI War Room"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Agentic AI Year in Review","url":"https://www.meetup.com/bay-area-bot-chat-and-conversational-app-developers/events/317519271/","description":"**Agentic AI Year in Review!**\nJoin us for an exciting evening discussing the top startup trends in Agentic AI of 2026 and predictions for 2027.\n\n**Featuring:**\n\n* [Shruti Merchant](https://www.linkedin.com/in/shrutimerchant/), Partner, Pear VC\n* [Tabish Gilani](https://www.linkedin.com/in/tabishgilani/), Product Growth Partner, a16z Speedrun\n* [Tracy Rubin](https://www.linkedin.com/in/tracy-rubin-a54439156/), Partner, Cooley LLP\n\n**Registration**\nTo attend, you need to [register at luma](https://luma.com/veyokv1b?utm_source=bachat) **<-** **Please register at Luma as the venue requires this.**\n\n**Agenda**\nDate: Tues December 8th, 5:00pm (**doors open at 5pm**)\nLocation: GitHub, 275 Brannan St, San Francisco (entrance on Brannan)\n\n* 5:00-6:00pm doors open for networking\n* 6:00-7:00pm panel discussion\n* 7:00-7:30pm additional networking\n\n**Want to demo?**\nIf you are interested in demoing at a future event, please fill out the [application form](https://forms.gle/ahzwgnAAs51pdiTQ9).","startDate":"2026-12-09T01:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"GitHub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"San Francisco","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"us","streetAddress":"275 Brannan St, San Francisco, CA"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Bay Area Chatbot, Voice Assistants, and Conversational AI","url":"https://www.meetup.com/bay-area-bot-chat-and-conversational-app-developers/"},"performer":"Bay Area Chatbot, Voice Assistants, and Conversational AI"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"SF CogSci #35: Ingressing Minds","url":"https://www.meetup.com/san-francisco-cognitive-science-meetup-group/events/316929501/","description":"Reading: Ingressing Minds: Causal, Non-Physical Patterns In-Form Natural, Synthetic, and Hybrid Embodiments by Michael Levin (2026). Read it [here](https://www.mdpi.com/2409-9287/11/5/161) ahead of the 15th.\n\nIf you're attending in person, please be sure to register [here](https://luma.com/sf-cogsci-35) as well, so you can get into the building.\n\nThank you!\n\nTom","startDate":"2026-12-16T03:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Frontier Tower 🧑‍🚀","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"San Francisco","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"us","streetAddress":"995 Market St, San Francisco, CA 94103, USA, San Francisco, CA"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"San Francisco Cognitive Science Reading Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/san-francisco-cognitive-science-meetup-group/"},"performer":"San Francisco Cognitive Science Reading Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"[SF] AI Builder Tour with Bluehost","url":"https://www.meetup.com/sv-enterprise-ai/events/317572865/","description":"**Important**: Registration on the[ ](https://www.aicamp.ai/event/eventdetails/W2026120306)[event website](https://www.aicamp.ai/event/eventdetails/W2026111709) is required for admission.\n(RSVP on meetup is turned off)\n\nJoin us for the Bluehost AI Builder Tour - San Francisco, an in-person experience bringing together entrepreneurs, developers, creators, and local AI builders ready to move from vision to launch and scale.\n\nWhether you're developing your next big idea, launching a business, or scaling something you've already built, this is your opportunity to connect with fellow builders, explore new possibilities, and get expert feedback.\n\n**Three awards, three chances to win awards - $30,000**:\nExplore three exciting opportunities to compete:\n\n* Build with Anything — Create an AI-powered solution using the tools of your choice.\n* Build & Win with Bluehost — Build a website or app using Bluehost AI Builder.\n* Vibeathon — Put your AI-powered creativity and building skills to the test.\n\n**What to Expect:**\n\n* Local AI Builder Showcases: Hear from local builders about their projects, challenges, and lessons learned.\n* Build, Host & Scale: Discover Bluehost innovations to help build, host, and run your projects.\n* Interactive AI Workshop: Bring your ideas or work in progress and get feedback from AI builders and experts.\n* Peer-to-Peer Breakouts: Discuss AI agents, infrastructure, performance, and costs with peers and experts.\n* Community & Networking: Connect with local AI builders, entrepreneurs, and industry experts.\n\n**Featured Speakers:**\n\n* Salim Ali, Bluehost\n* Antonis Papatsaras, Bluehost\n* Vishwa Shroff, Bluehost\n* Ana Ramdas, Build First\n* and more\n*\n\n**Agenda:**\n\n* 9:00am–9:30am: Coffee, Networking & Demos\n* 9:30am–10:00am: Welcome & Introduction\n* 10:00am–12:00pm: AI Builder Showcases & Workshop\n* 12:00pm–1:00pm: Lunch\n* 1:00pm–3:00pm: Interactive Workshop & Expert Feedback\n* 3:15pm–4:30pm: Peer Discussions & Expert Consultations\n* 5:00pm onwards: Happy Hour & Networking\n*","startDate":"2026-12-09T17:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Avalon","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"San Francisco","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"us","streetAddress":"1244 Sutter St, San Francisco, CA 94109, USA, San Francisco, CA"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Silicon Valley Enterprise AI","url":"https://www.meetup.com/sv-enterprise-ai/"},"performer":"Silicon Valley Enterprise AI"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Scaling Agentic AI in Drug Discovery","url":"https://www.meetup.com/baybifx/events/317528641/","description":"BayBifx & Ardigen present a night of exciting talks on AI in Drug Discovery, hosted by Myriad Genetics at its amazing SSF Nexus facility.\n\nPLEASE REGISTER ONLY THROUGH THE LINK BELOW:\nhttps://ardigen.com/scaling-agentic-ai-in-drug-discovery-event-2026/","startDate":"2026-12-16T01:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"233 East Grand Avenue","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"South San Francisco","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"us","streetAddress":"233 E Grand Ave., South San Francisco, CA 94080, USA, South San Francisco, CA"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Bay Area Bioinformatics Forum","url":"https://www.meetup.com/baybifx/"},"performer":"Bay Area Bioinformatics Forum"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"AI INFRASUMMIT 6","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-future-of-ai-entrepreneurship-venture/events/317557787/","description":"This event is organized by Ignite GTM.\n\nOur meetup group is collaborating by promoting this event.\n\nIn order to attend, please register here:\n\n[AI INFRA SUMMIT 6 · Luma](https://luma.com/aiinfra6?coupon=IPO20&tk=ZDbDIC)\n\nOur meetup members get 20 PERCENT OFF!\n\nUse promo code:\n\nIPO20\n\nHurry!\n\nSlots are limited!\n\nAI is no longer an experiment. It’s the infrastructure race shaping economic power, technological sovereignty, and the next decade of global growth.\n\n​AI INFRA SUMMIT 6 brings this conversation to San Francisco, the center of gravity for AI innovation and deployment. This is where the builders of the AI stack come together: founders, operators, investors, policymakers, and infrastructure leaders powering the next generation of compute, data centers, and intelligent systems.\n\n​From chips to clusters to agentic workloads, AIS6 focuses on the systems turning AI from promise into production.\n​If you’re building, funding, or scaling at the AI infrastructure layer, this is where you align with the ecosystem defining what comes next.\n\n***\n\n## ​**Who Attends**\n\n* ​AI-native founders and builders\n* ​Cloud and infrastructure providers\n* ​Investors, venture capitalists, and strategic partners\n* ​Energy, chip, and data center operators\n* ​Policy and ecosystem leaders\n\n***\n\n## ​**Event Details**\n\n​**Date:** Wednesday, December 9th, 2026\n**Location:** San Francisco\n**Time:** 8:30 a.m.–8:00 p.m. PT\n**Host:** IgniteGTM\n\nIf you would like to have a demo / marketing table, please send an email message to:\n\nsiliconvalleysponsor@gmail.com\n\nPut this in the subject header:\n\nW 12/9/26 - Tabler","startDate":"2026-12-09T16:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Midway","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"San Francisco","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"us","streetAddress":"900 Marin St, San Francisco, CA 94124, USA, San Francisco, CA"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"The future of AI, Entrepreneurship and Venture Capital","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-future-of-ai-entrepreneurship-venture/"},"performer":"The future of AI, Entrepreneurship and Venture Capital"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"AI Book Club: Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ai-builders-and-learners-sf/events/316685013/","description":"**Novembers's book is \"Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback\"!**\n\n​This is a casual-style event. Not a structured presentation on topics. Sometimes, the discussion even drifts away from the chapters, but feel free to grab the mic to help steer it back.\n\n​Feel free to join the discussion even if you have not read the book chapters! :)\n​Want to discuss the contents during the reading week? Join the AI Slack group: https://slack.flyte.org/\n​-------------------------------------------------\nAbout the book:\n\n* ​Title: **Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback**\n* ​Authors: Nathan Lambert\n* ​Published: August 2026\n\n​Manning (Promo code: AIBookClub should give you 45% off: [https://www.manning.com/books/reinforcement-learning-from-human-feedback](https://www.manning.com/books/reinforcement-learning-from-human-feedback?utm_source=luma)\n​O'rielly platform: [https://learning.oreilly.com/library/view/reinforcement-learning-from/9781633434301/](https://learning.oreilly.com/library/view/reinforcement-learning-from/9781633434301/?utm_source=luma)\n​\n​Chapters:\n\n* ​1 Introduction\n* ​2 A tiny history of RLHF\n* ​3 Training overview\n* ​4 Instruction fine-tuning\n* ​5 Reward modeling\n* ​6 Reinforcement learning\n* ​7 Reasoning and inference-time scaling\n* ​8 Direct-alignment algorithms\n* ​9 Rejection sampling\n* ​10 The nature of preferences\n* ​11 Preference data\n* ​12 Synthetic data\n* ​13 Tool use and function calling\n* ​14 Over-optimization\n* ​15 Regularization\n* ​16 Evaluation\n* ​17 Crafting model character and products\n\n​**Book Description**\n​***Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback: LLM alignment and post-training* helps you understand how modern AI models can be adapted to better match the needs and expectations of their users. Rather than surveying the vast field of reinforcement learning, elite AI researcher Nathan Lambert concentrates exclusively on RLHF and its immediate importance to post-training generative AI models.**\n\n**This compact book gets right to the point. Early chapters establish the training overview, explain instruction fine-tuning, and build reliable reward models. The middle chapters transition into the heart of alignment, exploring core policy gradient algorithms, Direct Preference Optimization (DPO), and inference-time scaling. Later chapters tackle the messy reality of data, guiding you through preference data collection, synthetic data generation, and the nuances of function calling.**","startDate":"2026-12-08T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OnlineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"VirtualLocation","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ai-builders-and-learners-sf/events/316685013/"},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"AI Builders and Learners SF","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ai-builders-and-learners-sf/"},"performer":"AI Builders and Learners SF"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Sales Funnels with Claude: See a Real One Opened Up, Page by Page [ONLINE]","url":"https://www.meetup.com/palo-alto-ai-business-vibes/events/317513615/","description":"A sales funnel used to take a copywriter, a designer, a developer and about three months. In this class Aida shows how her team now builds the offer, the pages and the follow-up emails with Claude in days, including for owners who don't have a product to sell yet.\n\nAida uses a well-known study on choice, a client example and her own team's funnel to show what a simple route from first click to repeat purchase looks like, then opens the real funnel and goes through it page by page.\n\n**What we'll cover:**\n• Why too many choices stop people buying, and what to remove first\n• The steps from stranger to repeat customer, and where most businesses stop\n• How a small first offer can cover the cost of finding a customer\n• Selling to the audience or network you already have, without ads\n• Using Claude to turn what you know into a first product\n• A real funnel opened up and explained page by page\n\n**Format:** An online class of about 60 minutes. Aida presents on screen, and our team answers questions in the chat.\n\n**Who it's for:** business owners, founders, coaches and service providers in Palo Alto and Silicon Valley who want customers to arrive more predictably. No marketing or technical background needed.\n\n**Bring:** a notebook, the link to your website or sales page if you have one, and one offer you sell or would like to sell.\n\n**Hosted by:** Aida from the Bridges Network.\n\n**When you RSVP:** three optional questions: one task you'd love AI to take off your plate, whether you would like a free AI consultation, and a phone number for an SMS reminder. Skip any you like.\n\n**Please note:** the last part introduces our team's done-for-you funnel service and invites anyone interested to book a call. Everything above is covered first.\n\n**Where:** Online, on our class page. The link appears here once you RSVP \"Going.\" The page asks for a name and email to let you in. No cost.","startDate":"2026-12-07T20:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OnlineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"VirtualLocation","url":"https://www.meetup.com/palo-alto-ai-business-vibes/events/317513615/"},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Palo Alto AI Business Vibes","url":"https://www.meetup.com/palo-alto-ai-business-vibes/"},"performer":"Palo Alto AI Business Vibes"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Build an Agentic AI Model Factory: Own Your AI","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ai-builders-and-learners-sf/events/317318556/","description":"​**Build a Sovereign AI Factory: an ML Engineer Agent that evaluates, fine-tunes, deploys, and improves open models.**\nRSVP on Luma for live link: https://luma.com/vfhq98ji\n\n​AI teams are starting to look beyond renting every capability from an external API, they're building systems they own and control. In this hands-on session we'll build exactly that by creating an ML Engineer Agent that will manage a model factory to select and fine-tune the best models for your applications.\n\n​We'll start with a walkthrough where we build an agent that evaluates open models in parallel, fine-tunes promising candidates, deploys the winner, and retrains automatically when performance drops. Think of it as the first brick in your own **model factory**: a repeatable system for evaluating, improving, and deploying models *you* control.\n\n​You'll see how [Union.ai](https://union.ai/?utm_source=luma) & Flyte give your AI workflows a **durable runtime** with *infrastructure as context,* so agents adapt infra resources, recover from failures, and keep moving without re-running completed work. And because it all runs in **your own cloud**, you own the full stack end to end: **your models, your data, your infrastructure, your IP.**","startDate":"2026-12-09T20:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OnlineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"VirtualLocation","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ai-builders-and-learners-sf/events/317318556/"},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"AI Builders and Learners SF","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ai-builders-and-learners-sf/"},"performer":"AI Builders and Learners SF"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Make Your GPU Earn Its Keep: A Kernel Engineering Deep Dive","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ai-performance-engineering/events/317171245/","description":"**Monday, November 30, 2026 · 9:00–10:00 AM PST · Online**\n**Zoom link:** [https://us02web.zoom.us/j/82308186562](https://us02web.zoom.us/j/82308186562)\nA powerful GPU can spend plenty of time waiting. What is it waiting for—and how do you find out?\n**Talk #0: Welcome and Meetup Updates**\nby Chris Fregly and Antje Barth\n**Talk #1: From “Why Is This Slow?” to a Faster Kernel**\nby Dr. Rajat “Raj” Dandekar, Co-founder of Vizuara\nJoin Raj for a focused tour of the engineering behind fast AI kernels, drawing on Vizuara’s Kernel Engineering course on Maven. We’ll connect the roofline model to CUDA execution and the GPU memory hierarchy, then look at how profiling guides optimizations such as coalesced memory access, tiling, and tensor-core use. Matrix multiplication and attention provide context for seeing how those ideas fit together in modern AI workloads, including FlashAttention.\nThe goal is a practical way to decide what to measure, which bottleneck matters, and whether an optimization helped. The session is dedicated to Raj’s talk, with time for audience questions.\n**Who it’s for:** Engineers comfortable with Python or basic PyTorch. Prior CUDA or C++ experience is not required.\n**Bio:** Dr. Rajat Dandekar is a co-founder of Vizuara and a Kernel Engineering course instructor. He holds a PhD in Mechanical Engineering from Purdue University and BTech and MTech degrees from IIT Madras.\n**Based on:** [Kernel Engineering: From CUDA Foundations to Frontier AI Kernels](https://maven.com/rajat-dandekar/kernel-engineering)\n**Zoom link:** [https://us02web.zoom.us/j/82308186562](https://us02web.zoom.us/j/82308186562)\n**Related Links**\nGithub Repo: [http://github.com/cfregly/ai-performance-engineering/](http://github.com/cfregly/ai-performance-engineering/)\nO’Reilly Book: [https://www.amazon.com/Systems-Performance-Engineering-Optimizing-Algorithms/dp/B0F47689K8/](https://www.amazon.com/Systems-Performance-Engineering-Optimizing-Algorithms/dp/B0F47689K8/)\nYouTube: [https://www.youtube.com/@AIPerformanceEngineering](https://www.youtube.com/@AIPerformanceEngineering)\nGenerative AI Free Course on DeepLearning.ai: [https://bit.ly/gllm](https://bit.ly/gllm)","startDate":"2026-11-30T17:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OnlineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"VirtualLocation","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ai-performance-engineering/events/317171245/"},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"AI Performance Engineering Meetup (San Francisco, Global)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ai-performance-engineering/"},"performer":"AI Performance Engineering Meetup (San Francisco, Global)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"AI Builders Thursdays | Weekly AI Demos, Talks & Networking","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ml-ai-learning-circle/events/316362930/","description":"🚀 **Build Your Own AI Chatbot with Python & OpenAI SDK!**\nYou’ve used ChatGPT, Claude, and other AI chatbots. **Now it’s time to build your own!**\nIn our next meetup, we’ll go beyond simply using AI tools and learn how to build a working AI chatbot using Python and the OpenAI API.\n💻 **We’ll start with a quick setup:**\n\n* Setting up your OpenAI API environment\n* Installing and using the OpenAI Python SDK\n* Connecting your Python application to an LLM\n\n🛠️ **Hands-On Lab: Build Your First GPT-Powered Chatbot!**\n**By the end of the session, you’ll have built your own AI chatbot from scratch using code—not just used ChatGPT or Claude!**\n✅ Beginner-friendly\n✅ Live coding and hands-on learning\n✅ Real-world AI development skills\n🔥 **Stop just using AI. Start building with AI!**\nDon’t miss this session! Come ready to code, learn, and build something exciting.\nSee you at the meetup! 🚀","startDate":"2026-11-27T03:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OnlineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"VirtualLocation","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ml-ai-learning-circle/events/316362930/"},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"AI Builders Community","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ml-ai-learning-circle/"},"performer":"AI Builders Community"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Local+Online Meetup: In-House ASR Architecture & Accurate Word Timestamps #001","url":"https://www.meetup.com/bay-area-voice-ai-happy-hours/events/317548418/","description":"Join fellow speech engineers, researchers, and voice AI builders in the South Bay for an evening of technical talks, paper deep dives, and casual networking!\n\n**Event Details**\n\n* **Who should come:** Voice AI researchers, engineers, and entrepreneurs\n* **When:** Every other Thursday, 6:30 PM – 8:30 PM\n* **Format:** Hybrid (in person at Hacker Dojo, plus online via **YouTube Live at https://www.youtube.com/@olewave** and Bilibili Live — direct stream links will be shared later)\n* **Cost:** Draft beer is free; $10 onsite food & drink chip-in for pizza and non-alcoholic beverages (free for students with valid ID)\n* **Food & drinks:** Draft beer, pizza, and non-alcoholic beverages provided\n\n**Agenda**\n**6:30 PM – 7:00 PM \\| Arrival & Open Networking** Grab a drink, meet fellow voice AI builders and researchers, and settle in.\n**7:00 PM – 8:00 PM \\| Main Program**\n\n* **7:00 PM – 7:05 PM:** **Voice AI News & Community Updates** (5 min)\n* **7:05 PM – 7:30 PM:** **Tech Share: Building In-House Voice AI Solutions - ASR - Part 1: Overview and Architecture** (20 min talk + 5 min Q&A) — Practical architecture, data, and deployment lessons learned from a speech AI veteran with more than 10 years of industry consulting experience.\n* **7:30 PM – 7:35 PM:** **Quick Break** (5 min) — Grab a drink refill and stretch before the paper walkthrough.\n* **7:35 PM – 8:00 PM:** **Paper Reading Deep Dive: Accurate ASR Word Timestamps** (20 min walkthrough + 5 min Q&A) — A walkthrough of **FA-Bench** and its open leaderboard, followed by a look at how **Olign** achieves high-precision word- and phone-level speech alignment.\n\n**8:00 PM – 8:30 PM \\| Happy Hour Mingle & Wrap\\-Up** Continue the conversation with the speaker, exchange contacts, and hang out until close.\n\n**About the Speaker**\n**Wei Chu** has more than 10 years of experience in building internal voice AI solutions to beat external tech-giant API vendors in accuracy, latency, and cost. He received his PhD in speech from the EE Department at UCLA and is the Founder and CEO of **Olewave**, which focuses on voice datasets, benchmarks, and solutions. He also hosts the Olewave Speech & NLP Paper Reading channel on YouTube (**[youtube.com/@olewave](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fyoutube.com%2F%40olewave)**) and organizes the Bay Area Voice AI Happy Hours Meetup (**[https://www.meetup.com/bay-area-voice-ai-happy-hours](https://www.meetup.com/bay-area-voice-ai-happy-hours)**). Outside of work, he likes soccer, fish cuisines, and traveling to learn languages, peoples, and cultures.\n\n**Location & How to Get There**\n**Venue:** Hacker Dojo **Address:** 3200 Patrick Henry Dr #250, Santa Clara, CA 95054 **Getting in:** Please use the main entrance with the automatic doors at 3200 Patrick Henry Dr.\n\n* **Driving & Parking:** Easily accessible via US-101 (exit Great America Pkwy / Bowers Ave) or CA-237 (exit Great America Pkwy). Free surface parking is available in the lot surrounding the building—look for Suite #250.\n* **Public Transit (VTA Light Rail & Caltrain):**\n* **VTA Light Rail:** Take the Orange Line to the **Great America Station** or **Old Ironsides Station**, both about a 10–15 minute walk from the venue.\n* **Caltrain + Transfer:** Take Caltrain to **Mountain View Station** and transfer to the VTA Orange Line toward Alum Rock, exiting at Great America Station (or take a \\~10-minute rideshare from Lawrence or Sunnyvale Caltrain stations).\n* **Biking:** Located right near the San Tomas Aquino Creek Trail for a direct, car-free bike commute from surrounding Silicon Valley neighborhoods.\n\n**Call for Volunteers**\nWe are looking for volunteers to help with check-in, A/V and livestream setup, and food/drink logistics! If you'd like to pitch in (volunteers get free admission and food), please message the organizers or reach out via Luma/Meetup.","startDate":"2026-12-04T02:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Bay Area Voice AI Happy Hours: Tech Share and Paper Reading","url":"https://www.meetup.com/bay-area-voice-ai-happy-hours/"},"performer":"Bay Area Voice AI Happy Hours: Tech Share and Paper Reading"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"[SF] AI Builder Tour with Bluehost","url":"https://www.meetup.com/sfbay-ai/events/317572861/","description":"**Important**: Registration on the[ ](https://www.aicamp.ai/event/eventdetails/W2026120306)[event website](https://www.aicamp.ai/event/eventdetails/W2026111709) is required for admission.\n(RSVP on meetup is turned off)\n\nJoin us for the Bluehost AI Builder Tour - San Francisco, an in-person experience bringing together entrepreneurs, developers, creators, and local AI builders ready to move from vision to launch and scale.\n\nWhether you're developing your next big idea, launching a business, or scaling something you've already built, this is your opportunity to connect with fellow builders, explore new possibilities, and get expert feedback.\n\n**Three awards, three chances to win awards - $30,000**:\nExplore three exciting opportunities to compete:\n\n* Build with Anything — Create an AI-powered solution using the tools of your choice.\n* Build & Win with Bluehost — Build a website or app using Bluehost AI Builder.\n* Vibeathon — Put your AI-powered creativity and building skills to the test.\n\n**What to Expect:**\n\n* Local AI Builder Showcases: Hear from local builders about their projects, challenges, and lessons learned.\n* Build, Host & Scale: Discover Bluehost innovations to help build, host, and run your projects.\n* Interactive AI Workshop: Bring your ideas or work in progress and get feedback from AI builders and experts.\n* Peer-to-Peer Breakouts: Discuss AI agents, infrastructure, performance, and costs with peers and experts.\n* Community & Networking: Connect with local AI builders, entrepreneurs, and industry experts.\n\n**Featured Speakers:**\n\n* Salim Ali, Bluehost\n* Antonis Papatsaras, Bluehost\n* Vishwa Shroff, Bluehost\n* Ana Ramdas, Build First\n* and more\n*\n\n**Agenda:**\n\n* 9:00am–9:30am: Coffee, Networking & Demos\n* 9:30am–10:00am: Welcome & Introduction\n* 10:00am–12:00pm: AI Builder Showcases & Workshop\n* 12:00pm–1:00pm: Lunch\n* 1:00pm–3:00pm: Interactive Workshop & Expert Feedback\n* 3:15pm–4:30pm: Peer Discussions & Expert Consultations\n* 5:00pm onwards: Happy Hour & Networking\n*","startDate":"2026-12-09T17:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Avalon","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"San Francisco","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"us","streetAddress":"1244 Sutter St, San Francisco, CA 94109, USA, San Francisco, CA"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"SF AI","url":"https://www.meetup.com/sfbay-ai/"},"performer":"SF AI"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Agentic AI Year in Review","url":"https://www.meetup.com/bay-area-research-in-nlp-and-ml/events/317519279/","description":"**Agentic AI Year in Review!**\nJoin us for an exciting evening discussing the top startup trends in Agentic AI of 2026 and predictions for 2027.\n\n**Featuring:**\n\n* [Shruti Merchant](https://www.linkedin.com/in/shrutimerchant/), Partner, Pear VC\n* [Tabish Gilani](https://www.linkedin.com/in/tabishgilani/), Product Growth Partner, a16z Speedrun\n* [Tracy Rubin](https://www.linkedin.com/in/tracy-rubin-a54439156/), Partner, Cooley LLP\n\n**Registration**\nTo attend, you need to [register at luma](https://luma.com/veyokv1b?utm_source=nlp) **<-** **Please register at Luma as the venue requires this.**\n\n**Agenda**\nDate: Tues December 8th, 5:00pm (**doors open at 5pm**)\nLocation: GitHub, 275 Brannan St, San Francisco (entrance on Brannan)\n\n* 5:00-6:00pm doors open for networking\n* 6:00-7:00pm panel discussion\n* 7:00-7:30pm additional networking\n\n**Want to demo?**\nIf you are interested in demoing at a future event, please fill out the [application form](https://forms.gle/ahzwgnAAs51pdiTQ9).","startDate":"2026-12-09T01:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"GitHub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"San Francisco","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"us","streetAddress":"275 Brannan St, San Francisco, CA"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Bay Area Research in NLP and ML","url":"https://www.meetup.com/bay-area-research-in-nlp-and-ml/"},"performer":"Bay Area Research in NLP and ML"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"ISCI 2026 - Agentic AI: From Hype to Reality","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ieee_cis_scv/events/317228051/","description":"***\n\nJoin us for the **International Symposium on Computational Intelligence (ISCI) 2026**, a premier virtual half-day event on Agentic AI: From Hype to Reality, broadly covering what it takes to build, trust, and stand behind AI agents in real-world use. The symposium brings together researchers and practitioners to discuss how agentic AI works in practice.\n**What to Expect**\n\n* **Expert Presentations** \\- 30\\-45 minute talks from internationally recognized speakers\n* **Interactive Q&A Sessions** \\- 15\\-minute Q&A following each presentation\n* **Global Perspective** \\- Speakers from Australia\\, India and beyond\n* **Live Streaming** \\- Real\\-time access via zoom\n\n**Talks & Speakers**\n\n* **Enough of scaling laws! Let's focus on downscaling** - Prof. Tanmoy Chakraborty, IIT Delhi, India\n* **AI Agents to Agentic AI: From Historical Perspective** \\- Prof\\. Dipankar Dasgupta\\, The University of Memphis\\, US\n* **From Learning to Unlearning: Building Secure and Trustworthy AI Agents for the AGI Era** - Prof. Danda B. Rawat, Howard University, Washington, US\n* **On the Possibility and Impossibility of Trusted Agentic Artificial Intelligence** \\- Prof\\. Hussein Abbass\\, University of New South Wales\\, Australia\n\nMore details at: https://events.vtools.ieee.org/m/589225","startDate":"2026-11-28T16:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OnlineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"VirtualLocation","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ieee_cis_scv/events/317228051/"},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"IEEE Computational Intelligence Society - SCV Chapter","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ieee_cis_scv/"},"performer":"IEEE Computational Intelligence Society - SCV Chapter"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"The Context Layer: Where Inference Gets Won or Lost in 2027","url":"https://www.meetup.com/venturebeat-ai-impact-series-sf/events/317461038/","description":"**About the Topic:**\n​2026 was the year the industry stopped counting tokens and started counting what they produced. First came tokenmaxxing, then the discipline of cost per task, and now a harder question is surfacing in every serious AI program: once you’ve made inference efficient, where do you spend what you freed up? The answer increasingly isn’t more GPUs. It’s context. Agents don’t answer prompts; they complete tasks across hundreds of steps, and at every step they need persistent, accurate, fast-to-reach, and affordable working memory. That memory has to live somewhere between the GPU and the data layer, and most enterprises haven’t yet decided where it lives, who owns it, or how to measure whether it’s working.\n\n​This salon brings together the practitioners furthest along in building that layer: the neoclouds already hitting the wall, the enterprises just arriving at it, and the infrastructure leaders defining what the context layer should be. Expect a frank conversation about the trade-offs between memory, data access, and GPU time, the new measures replacing utilization, and the emerging best practices for an inference year that starts in January.\n\n**​Featured Speakers:**\n\n* Aanchal Gupta, CSO, Adobe\n* ​Liran Zvibel, CEO and Co-Founder of WEKA\n\n**​Participate in the Conversation:**\nLink to register: https://luma.com/hv2l9g51\n\n​Request your seat today. Space is intentionally limited to keep the room small and the conversation real. This is an in-person only event.\n\n​NOTE: It can take up to 24 hours for reservation processing. Please also check your spam mail for email from VentureBeat regarding the event.","startDate":"2026-12-11T01:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"San Francisco","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"San Francisco","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"us","streetAddress":"San Francisco, CA, USA, San Francisco, CA"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"VentureBeat AI Impact Series - SF","url":"https://www.meetup.com/venturebeat-ai-impact-series-sf/"},"performer":"VentureBeat AI Impact Series - SF"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"AI INFRA SUMMIT","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-izengajf/events/317557797/","description":"This event is organized by Ignite GTM.\n\nOur meetup group is collaborating by promoting this event.\n\nIn order to attend, please register here:\n\n[AI INFRA SUMMIT 6 · Luma](https://luma.com/aiinfra6?coupon=IPO20&tk=ZDbDIC)\n\nOur meetup members get 20 PERCENT OFF!\n\nUse promo code:\n\nIPO20\n\nHurry!\n\nSlots are limited!\n\nAI is no longer an experiment. It’s the infrastructure race shaping economic power, technological sovereignty, and the next decade of global growth.\n\n​AI INFRA SUMMIT 6 brings this conversation to San Francisco, the center of gravity for AI innovation and deployment. This is where the builders of the AI stack come together: founders, operators, investors, policymakers, and infrastructure leaders powering the next generation of compute, data centers, and intelligent systems.\n\n​From chips to clusters to agentic workloads, AIS6 focuses on the systems turning AI from promise into production.\n​If you’re building, funding, or scaling at the AI infrastructure layer, this is where you align with the ecosystem defining what comes next.\n\n***\n\n## ​**Who Attends**\n\n* ​AI-native founders and builders\n* ​Cloud and infrastructure providers\n* ​Investors, venture capitalists, and strategic partners\n* ​Energy, chip, and data center operators\n* ​Policy and ecosystem leaders\n\n***\n\n## ​**Event Details**\n\n​**Date:** Wednesday, December 9th, 2026\n**Location:** San Francisco\n**Time:** 8:30 a.m.–8:00 p.m. PT\n**Host:** IgniteGTM\n\nIf you would like to have a demo / marketing table, please send an email message to:\n\nsiliconvalleysponsor@gmail.com\n\nPut this in the subject header:\n\nW 12/9/26 - Tabler","startDate":"2026-12-09T16:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Midway","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"San Francisco","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"us","streetAddress":"900 Marin St, San Francisco, CA 94124, USA, San Francisco, CA"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Sunnyvale Data Science Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-izengajf/"},"performer":"Sunnyvale Data Science Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Weekly paper review, coding project, or random discussion","url":"https://www.meetup.com/west-coast-machine-learning-meetup/events/315814934/","description":"This is a placeholder for our weekly meeting. We will update the meeting description each week to include the topic of the week. Stay tuned :)\n\nEvery week we meet (virtually) and discuss the most interesting topics in AI, ML and Deep Learning.\nWe usually rotate weeks so that every other week one of the members presents a deep learning/machine learning paper, frequently paired with a video explaining the concepts. In the off weeks, we present information about different projects. We cover computer vision, language (LLM's), health/hard science and generative models (Diffusion, GAN's etc.).\nPeople of all levels of skill are welcome--from newbies to machine learning, to PhD's in DL/ML/AI.\nWe have been meeting for over 6 years weekly and have developed a neat pace and community--and all are welcome. Come join us and stay abreast of the biggest topics in Artificial Intelligence.","startDate":"2026-11-27T02:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OnlineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"VirtualLocation","url":"https://www.meetup.com/west-coast-machine-learning-meetup/events/315814934/"},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"West Coast Machine Learning Meetup (aka East Bay/Trivalley)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/west-coast-machine-learning-meetup/"},"performer":"West Coast Machine Learning Meetup (aka East Bay/Trivalley)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"GPU, CUDA, and PyTorch Performance Optimizations","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ai-performance-engineering/events/314093502/","description":"**Zoom link**: [https://us02web.zoom.us/j/82308186562](https://us02web.zoom.us/j/82308186562)\n\n**Talk #0: Introductions and Meetup Updates**\nby Chris Fregly and Antje Barth\n\n**Talk #1: GPU, PyTorch, and CUDA Performance Optimizations**\n\n**Talk #2: GPU, PyTorch, and CUDA Performance Optimizations**\n\n**Zoom link**: [https://us02web.zoom.us/j/82308186562](https://us02web.zoom.us/j/82308186562)\n\n**Related Links**\nGithub Repo: [http://github.com/cfregly/ai-performance-engineering/](http://github.com/cfregly/ai-performance-engineering/)\nO'Reilly Book: [https://www.amazon.com/Systems-Performance-Engineering-Optimizing-Algorithms/dp/B0F47689K8/](https://www.amazon.com/Systems-Performance-Engineering-Optimizing-Algorithms/dp/B0F47689K8/)\nYouTube: [https://www.youtube.com/@AIPerformanceEngineering](https://www.youtube.com/@AIPerformanceEngineering)\nGenerative AI Free Course on DeepLearning.ai: [https://bit.ly/gllm](https://bit.ly/gllm)","startDate":"2026-12-14T17:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OnlineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"VirtualLocation","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ai-performance-engineering/events/314093502/"},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"AI Performance Engineering Meetup (San Francisco, Global)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ai-performance-engineering/"},"performer":"AI Performance Engineering Meetup (San Francisco, Global)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"AI INFRA SUMMIT 6","url":"https://www.meetup.com/silicon-valley-machine-learning-learners-and-entrepreneurs/events/317557255/","description":"This event is organized by Ignite GTM.\n\nOur meetup group is collaborating by promoting this event.\n\nIn order to attend, please register here:\n\n[AI INFRA SUMMIT 6 · Luma](https://luma.com/aiinfra6?coupon=IPO20&tk=ZDbDIC)\n\nOur meetup members get 20 PERCENT OFF!\n\nUse promo code:\n\nIPO20\n\nHurry!\n\nSlots are limited!\n\nAI is no longer an experiment. It’s the infrastructure race shaping economic power, technological sovereignty, and the next decade of global growth.\n\n​AI INFRA SUMMIT 6 brings this conversation to San Francisco, the center of gravity for AI innovation and deployment. This is where the builders of the AI stack come together: founders, operators, investors, policymakers, and infrastructure leaders powering the next generation of compute, data centers, and intelligent systems.\n\n​From chips to clusters to agentic workloads, AIS6 focuses on the systems turning AI from promise into production.\n​If you’re building, funding, or scaling at the AI infrastructure layer, this is where you align with the ecosystem defining what comes next.\n\n***\n\n## ​**Who Attends**\n\n* ​AI-native founders and builders\n* ​Cloud and infrastructure providers\n* ​Investors, venture capitalists, and strategic partners\n* ​Energy, chip, and data center operators\n* ​Policy and ecosystem leaders\n\n***\n\n## ​**Event Details**\n\n​**Date:** Wednesday, December 9th, 2026\n**Location:** San Francisco\n**Time:** 8:30 a.m.–8:00 p.m. PT\n**Host:** IgniteGTM\n\nIf you would like to have a demo / marketing table, please send an email message to:\n\nsiliconvalleysponsor@gmail.com\n\nPut this in the subject he